{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"signalingNaN","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default IEEE 754 behavior of operations involving a signaling NaN is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to raise the Invalid flag in the floating-point environment and return a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"quiet NaN.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Operations on types conforming to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FloatingPoint"},{"text":" protocol should","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"support this behavior, but they might also support other options. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, it would be reasonable to implement alternative operations in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which operating on a signaling NaN triggers a runtime error or results","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in a diagnostic for debugging purposes. Types that implement alternative","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behaviors for a signaling NaN must document the departure.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Other than these signaling operations, a signaling NaN behaves in the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same manner as a quiet NaN."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/FloatingPoint\/signalingNaN","interfaceLanguage":"